sentences.l:
Zilu asked about government.
The Master said: “Go before them;
toil for them.”

If affairs are not accomplished, the rites and music do not flourish;
if the rites and music do not flourish, punishments and penalties do not hit the mark;
if punishments and penalties do not hit the mark, the people have nowhere to set hand or foot.

If those above love the rites, none of the people dare be irreverent;
if those above love what is right, none of the people dare not submit;
if those above love good faith, none of the people dare not bring out their true feelings.
Now if it is like this,
the people of the four quarters will come carrying their children in slings on their backs —
what use is grain-growing?

The Master said: “He recites the Odes, all three hundred;
hand him government, and he does not get through;
send him to the four quarters, and he cannot answer on his own:
though it be much,
what use is it?”

The Master said: “If there were one who would employ me,
a full round of months, no more, and it would pass;
three years, and it would be accomplished.”

People's saying goes:
“Being lord — hard;
being minister — not easy.”

Zixia, being steward of Jufu, asked about government.
The Master said: “Do not want speed;
do not have your eye on small gains.
Want speed, and you do not get through;
have your eye on small gains, and great matters are not brought to completion.”

Fan Chi asked about humaneness.
The Master said: “Dwelling at home, respectful;
handling affairs, reverent;
with others, wholehearted.
Even if you go to the Yi and Di,
these cannot be cast aside.”

He said: “May I venture to ask about the next?”
He said: “His lineage and clan speak of him as filial;
his district and village speak of him for deference.”

The Master said: “With the gentleman, serving is easy and pleasing hard.
Please him not by the Way, and he is not pleased;
come to his employing others, and he uses each as a vessel.
With the small man, serving is hard and pleasing easy.
Please him, even not by the Way, and he is pleased;
come to his employing others, and he seeks completeness in them.”
